{"name":"Tostada","hex":"#e3c19c","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"tostada","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A flat tortilla that has been fried or toasted, or a dish based on this, usually associated with the cuisine of Latin America.","A bowl-shaped tortilla that has been fried and filled with various ingredients."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tostada"}],"entries":[{"title":"Tostada (toast)","blocks":[{"text":"Tostada is a Spanish word which literally means \"toasted\". It is used in some Hispanic American countries to name several different traditional local dishes which have in common that they are toasted or use a toasted ingredient as the main base of their preparation."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4d/Caf%C3%A9_con_leche_and_tostadas.jpg/330px-Caf%C3%A9_con_leche_and_tostadas.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tostada_(toast)","wikidata":"Q7827887"},{"title":"Tostada (tortilla)","blocks":[{"text":"Tostadas are various dishes in Mexican and Guatemalan cuisine based on toasted tortillas."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/05/Atun_tostadas_%2843015501031%29.jpg/330px-Atun_tostadas_%2843015501031%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tostada_(tortilla)","wikidata":"Q3280441"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c2/Tostadas_shrimp_cooking_food_dinner_salsa.jpg/500px-Tostadas_shrimp_cooking_food_dinner_salsa.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c2/Tostadas_shrimp_cooking_food_dinner_salsa.jpg/500px-Tostadas_shrimp_cooking_food_dinner_salsa.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Shrimp tostada","link":"https://en.wi